{"kind":"report","text":"Approve CLI JSON design revision5 at exact8108b8f6f8df54bd36ad23bc50ed9182fa8a6e48/treeb710717aaaf9379eefc989efaf0af8d26b44f76e. The sole primary notes/2026-10-12-cli-json-output-design.md was read in full, together with the exact revision4-to5 diff. No remaining blocking design findings.\n\nReview764cf535's storage prerequisite finding is resolved. Section7 now correctly states that current Store.private/files.ts lacks bounded owner/symlink admission, progress lock/CAS and crash guarantees. It requires a new ReadProgressStore and new filesystem witnesses. Its short cross-process critical sections protect admission/current revision and successor commit, an exact owned in-flight reservation fences the intervening remote reads, and a competing invocation cannot replace it. Descriptor identity/size and bounded actual reads precede parsing. The admitted snapshot and revision pointer must be flushed/committed before releasing a token. Uncertain/orphaned work is not credited, restart is limited to the owned read operation, and actual platform filesystem/lock recovery remains an implementation review obligation. Atomic rename is no longer presented as serialization or crash durability.\n\nPrior0fb944f7 F1/F2 stay resolved: authenticated producer-owned retained progress, not submitted counters/cursors/checkpoints, supports cumulative coverage; an actual rolling tail supports limit20 when only five entries remain. The fixed pre-admitted terminal result, 8MiB snapshot/16MiB operation bounds, revision checks, expiry and no-unadvanceable-token rule state truthful finite failure behavior. They are specified requirements, not passing implementation evidence.\n\nExplicit design adoption remains: one typed execution with text/JSON adapters; native answers, receipts and later observation/custody evidence survive every phase; safe public error construction precedes serialization; option-value ownership is preserved. Adopt the finite JSON MCP usage/2 exception